    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d768">

                <pb facs="0934" n="840" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg840"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">411.58J63/52</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Swedish Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Boström</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Cotton</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-17">October 17, 1930</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Cotton</hi>: With reference to your
                    letter of July 1st last, concerning submission to a neutral tribunal of the
                    claim of my Government against the United States for ship-detention damages
                    during the war, and to my preliminary answer of July 2nd,<anchor n="18"
                        xml:id="d768-f1"/> I have the honour to inform you that I have discussed the
                    matter with my Government and that I am ready to discuss with you the terms of
                    submission and the personnel of the tribunal.</p>
                <p>I beg to transmit herewith a draft of the main points of a compromise, drawn up
                    by our Foreign Office, and will be glad to discuss the whole matter with you
                    orally.</p>
                <p>Very sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Boström</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d768-a1.xml" xpointer="d768-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
